+/*
+ * Redwood (the Exynos 990 port's Metal): what the cache keeps, and what it did. CoreAnimation makes its
+ * offscreen targets in bursts 5-25 s apart and keeps them 1-4 s (PLANS/10-mali2metal.md, run 19), so with
+ * upstream's "drop what has been idle 2 s" every burst found the cache empty and paid an allocation and a
+ * mapping in the kernel per texture. Here an idle BO is kept up to REDWOOD_BO_IDLE_S seconds, and the cache
